{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1441 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "283a9f961179ed71da2d4bd7caa0aeaab04212b9a78ab0b828e4d974f0f7af32" :edb/db-before-t 1440 :edb/db-after-t 1441 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534753 50 #inst "2026-10-12T10:46:44.765Z" 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186115249 1038 #edb/ref 17592186435080 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186124499 1038 #edb/ref 17592186435081 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186160970 1075 #edb/ref 17592186160975 13194139534753 17592186045417 false] [17592186160970 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435070 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186160970 1078 #edb/ref 17592186160973 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186162613 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186162613 1071 "Which of the following matrices are symmetric?\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,R=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 8 \\\\ 8 & -5\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186162613 1071 "Which of the following matrices are symmetric?\n\n$P = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}, Q = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}, R = \\begin{bmatrix}5 & 8 \\\\ 8 & -5\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139534753 17592186045417 false] [17592186162613 1074 "A square matrix $A$ is symmetric if it is equal to its transpose:\n\n$$\nA={A}^{T}\n$$\n\nEquivalently, ${a}_{ij}={a}_{ji}$ for all $i,j.$ In other words, $A$ is symmetric across its main diagonal. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- $P$ is a symmetric matrix. Indeed, $P={P}^{T}.$\n\n- $Q$ is *not* a symmetric matrix. Since ${q}_{12}\\ne {q}_{21},$ we obtain $Q\\ne {Q}^{T}.$\n\n$$\nQ=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- $R$ is a symmetric matrix. Indeed, $R={R}^{T}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$P$ and $R$ only.\"" 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186172093 1038 #edb/ref 17592186435082 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186304939 1071 "Which of the following first-order linear differential equations are homogeneous?\n\n- ${y}^{′}+7xy=5$\n- ${y}^{′}+7xy=0$\n- ${y}^{′}+7xy=-2y$" 13194139534753 17592186045417 false] [17592186304939 1071 "Which of the following first-order linear differential equations are homogeneous?\n\nI. ${y}^{′}+7xy=5$\n\nII. ${y}^{′}+7xy=0$\n\nIII. ${y}^{′}+7xy=-2y$" 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435060 1043 #edb/ref 17592186435083 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435060 1043 #edb/ref 17592186435084 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435060 1043 #edb/ref 17592186435085 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435060 1043 #edb/ref 17592186435086 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435060 1043 #edb/ref 17592186435087 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435060 1043 #edb/ref 17592186435088 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435060 1043 #edb/ref 17592186435089 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435060 1043 #edb/ref 17592186435090 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435060 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045460 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435060 1045 "Quiz 7" 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435060 1046 #edb/ref 17592186435088 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435060 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046659 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435060 1053 #uuid "bb107373-be8d-5258-84bf-9e57da002e0b" 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435061 1080 "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1}" 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435061 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435061 1083 #uuid "1d53923c-6f45-51dc-ae6c-80093cc282ad" 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435062 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435062 108