7592186435077 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435061 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435077 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435065 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435077 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435072 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435077 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435073 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435077 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435076 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435077 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435077 1077 "selection" 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435077 1078 #edb/ref 17592186435073 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435077 1079 #uuid "1b9000ab-e8bd-5f5c-84a8-8cef429e6f0b" 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435078 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435066 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435078 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435067 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435078 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435069 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435078 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435074 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435078 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435075 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435078 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435078 1077 "selection" 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435078 1078 #edb/ref 17592186435069 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435078 1079 #uuid "3d3eb90b-b341-501f-a49e-f9c67d7e1ee8" 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435079 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435062 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435079 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435063 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435079 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435064 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435079 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435068 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435079 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435071 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435079 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435079 1077 "selection" 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435079 1078 #edb/ref 17592186435063 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435079 1079 #uuid "9fdab432-8653-5165-9ae6-72fb1a348731" 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435080 1068 #edb/ref 17592186435077 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435080 1069 "q-132004" 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435080 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435080 1071 "The inverse of the matrix $N$ is found using row operations, as shown below. What are the row operations corresponding to the blank spaces?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[N\\,|\\,I] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435080 1072 #uuid "4527164d-e7cb-52d0-bbe2-36d132296780" 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435080 1074 "We write down $N$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $N$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[N\\,|\\,I] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding row operations are\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}↔\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2}.\n$$\n\nThe matrix ${N}^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{N}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435081 1068 #edb/ref 17592186435079 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435081 1069 "q-70713" 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435081 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435081 1071 "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=t-2 \\\\ y=2-3t \\\\ z=2t-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind a vector that is parallel to the line." 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435081 1072 #uuid "8744c31a-0769-5670-8154-7878dd8f3f11" 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435081 1074 "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}t-2 \\\\ 2-3t \\\\ 2t-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ -3t \\\\ 2t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ \\,2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nThis implies that the straight line passes through the point $(-2,2,-1)$  and is parallel to the vector $v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435082 1068 #edb/ref 17592186435078 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435082 1069 "q-124296" 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435082 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435082 1071 "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=6u+4v+2,\\,y=5v-1\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6 & a \\\\ 0 & b\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435082 1072 #uuid "fba38d94-94f1-5e40-9342-c81f8eabc355" 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435082 1074 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6u+4v+2 \\\\ 5v-1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6u+4v+2 \\\\ 5v-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6u+4v \\\\ 5v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=4+5+(-1)=8.\n$$" 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435083 1062 #uuid "0e975a13-b456-5602-b4a4-86ab4d7bf99f" 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435083 1063 #edb/ref 17592186162613 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435084 1058 #edb/ref 17592186435086 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435084 1062 #uuid "16085287-bd7c-5cbe-86ad-7e35c6ecbe2d" 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435084 1063 #edb/ref 17592186435082 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435085 1058 #edb/ref 17592186435084 13194139534753 17592186045417 true] [17592186435085 1062 #uuid "227e9481-f504-5749-ab7b-6ee925602a24" 13194139534